## Findings

- Smooth: trapezoid and Simpson reach orders 2 and 4. Gauss-Legendre 4 hits the 1e-14 floor by n = 8 (5.7e-15), leaving n = 2, 4; their fit gives 8.2358, consistent with 8 but a two-point estimate (see footnote).
- Romberg on exp(-x^2) reaches the 1e-14 floor from n = 64 (1.5e-16 at n = 1024); Gauss-Legendre 4 reaches it earlier (n = 8) but uses 4 evaluations per panel.
- Singular: all rules show order about 4/3 (Romberg 1.3465, close to but not equal to 4/3), set by the x^(1/3) endpoint singularity. Constants differ: at n = 1024 the errors are 2.68e-5 (trapezoid), 1.15e-5 (Romberg), 5.26e-6 (Simpson), 1.89e-7 (Gauss), i.e. Simpson and Gauss are 5x and 140x below trapezoid at equal panel count, though cost per panel also differs (about 1, 2, 4 new evaluations).
- Float64 errors; the 1e-14 cutoff keeps fits clear of rounding. Orders are empirical fits over k = 1..10, not proofs.
